    "questionText": "If $f(x) = 2x + 3$, find the inverse function $f^{-1}(x)$.",
    "questionType": "multiple_choice",
    "options": [
      "$f^{-1}(x) = 2x - 3$",
      "$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{2}{x - 3}$",
      "$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x + 3}{2}$",
      "$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{2}$"
    ],
    "correctAnswer": "$f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{2}$",
    "explanation": {
      "overview": "Set $y = 2x + 3$. Rearrange for $x$: $y - 3 = 2x \\implies x = \\frac{y - 3}{2}$. Replace $y$ with $x$: $f^{-1}(x) = \\frac{x - 3}{2}$.",
      "stepByStep": [
        "Set y = f(x).",
        "Isolate x.",
        "Swap x and y."
      ],
      "keyConcept": "Inverse functions.",
      "commonMistakes": [
        "Forgetting to replace y with x."
      ],
      "examTip": "Inverse function undoes the original function."
    }
